  "id": "higher-order-design",
  "term": "higher order design",
  "definition": "In the PAL-D framework for film and television, higher-order design refers to broad scene-design dimensions that organize more specific formal choices to shape the viewer’s predictive and emotional experience over time. The article describes four such dimensions: sensory density, framing and focus, narrative-contextual cueing, and affective-empathic cueing.",
